ntion and accuracy. Not good.\n\nCandidate A: reliability and decision, but communication difficulty could be serious for cockpit. Egocentric may affect crew.\n\nCandidate B: stress and technical, but uncooperative could be serious.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility and problem solving, but arrogance and weak leadership may affect crew.\n\nWe need to decide initial recommendation. Perhaps Candidate C is strongest overall despite concerns, because anticipation and leadership are critical for long-distance flights. But we need to justify.\n\nLet's propose recommendation: Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: can anticipate dangerous situations, very good leadership qualities, but can be unorganized and not good at taking criticism.\n\nWe also need to reference that we are starting discussion. That's okay.\n\nNow produce output."}
